r, or conversely, being away from there should healthem slower (since we want to reduce the healing, not increase it).Dave**airborne**To: manglaFwd:  healingCc: archesDate: Nov  1To: airborneRe:   healingCc: archesDate: Oct 31I don't know that we should remove all meditation outside of a 'temple' butmaybe we could reduce the healing rate outside of that player's guild rooms.Seems to me that being in their temple, or at their shrine, or whatever,should heal them faster, or conversely, being away from there should healthem slower (since we want to reduce the healing, not increase it).Dave**airborne**To: manglaSubj: healing...Cc: archesDate: Nov  1Sorry about that, zigged when I should have zagged.Here's the idea that I have been bouncing about in my head.  Ok, suppose we limit meditation/healing skills to only the guild roomand \"shrines\".  Then we give guild members the ability to create shrines in various locations.  Players will be able to have their healing, but they would have to work a bit for it.  To start, we'd have the shrine needed to be built.  An easy way toget players to spend a bunch of gold on all sorts of things, bowls, statues, insense, etc.  Then they would have to protect those locationsonce they were built.  Certainly leaving lots of valuables laying around would tempt almost any player, which would kinda be the point.Add in the idea that some elements of theshrine would degrade withtime (insence comes to mind) and have to be replaced every so often.  The idea is to create an economy by finding reasons for players to gatheror purchase things that aren't just for killing.  If insence were onlyavailable in a small handful of locations, and there was a demand for itwe'd create the demand.  It helps control healing rates, keeps moneydown a bit, adds a roleplaying element to the mud, and encourages guildsto work together.Ideas and critics?**tatsuo**To: manglaSubj: reopen ezo and ishikawa