 can afford to be relaxed a little.  The two options are you give them basic directions and hope they find someweapons or something or you log off your wiz character and comeon with your player character and hope they don't associate the two.It may sound like an alien concept, but there are people who don'tknow that \"n\" is an abbreviation for \"north\".  I came in on thisguy having a conversation with the Paperboy.In my opinion (and I'm not suggesting this as a \"norm\", I'm a verylenient person anyway...) there is no harm in a wiz helping a newbieget up to level 5, provided there's no cloning of weapons, nogiving away of money (even then, what's the harm in 1000 coins?)and no quest hints invovled.  If anything, having a wiz help a newbie SHOULD turn them into a good player.(get them into the habit of examining things in rooms, etc.).OK, we should be concentrating on coding or something wizlike.But what's the point in coding if no-one's gonna be around toenjoy the code.Other stuff?  Ohhh there's plenty of other stuff, trust me :-)But it can wait.If you're dead set against this idea, I understand why.It goes against everything we've ever been taught aboutwizplayer interaction.If not then congratulations!You've just had a \"playerkeeping\" idea!Get it implemented!Do it unexpectedly!Watch everyone run around in circles of confusion!Your mentee,RedsexyPS I've also made some brief posts about the MUD on various sitesand bulletin boards.  I've noticed a LOT more newbies today.This is what we're aiming for, yes?**mangla**To: tatsuoSubj: ezo coastCc: archesDate: Mar  9I had to fix up players/tatsuo/ezo/coast/genCoast.cthis morning. This is the second day in a row thatareas of Ezo would not load. Please be more careful whenchanging things. All errors are simple. Missing ;or extra \" and in this case one of the problems wasa function redefinition.-Mangla**turbo**To: manglaSubj: /p/turbo/obj/raise_rod.cDate: 