e archand i am consistantly put off and ignored.  The arches want to do everything behind closed doors.  I am sending this letter to Mangla, who of all the arches, is theonly one that codes, and has been here, and who has admittedly pointed out thathe forgets things, and misses things, because of everything that needs done.Coding for HM is something that I enjoy to the fullest, but it has not been fun.At every turn I have an archwizard speaking down at me, lying about me or atleast continuing an untrue rumor to others, THIS IS LOGGED, I have sent it to mangla.  We have archwizards who last coded 5 years ago.  We have archwizardswith outside commitments that take up space here.  We have archwizards thattake off 5 months and turn up like messiahs reasserting their rightful positionsand casting down judgements. And we have one coding arch.For 3 and one half years I watched the mud go through death throws, as playersand wizards were driven off by shitty policies, guild closings, and the mudbeing moved around( all reasons I have heard).  Sauron, of the belovedninja guild had 3.5 years to recode ninja, he also had 3.5 years toput the monk into a bin system, and do something to balance it.  It just wasn'tdone.  I do not know what he has done, but i can only speak of what wasn't done,and ask if opening and fixing these guilds was less important that what was done.There was plenty of time for these people to \"shit or get off the pot\".It wasn't done.  For those of you who do not know, or who have prescribed tothe rumors that abound.  I was banned by mistake.  I was kept away and putoff without reason.  Untrustworty was heard. All sorts of things.For the brief time i was unbanned, i was NEVER returned to my position,although it was a mistake that i lost it.  I was kept and treated asa wiz with suspicion, and comments being made about me.  It sucked.I was restored to my position.  Airborne said it was a check on Mangla.Mangla said it was to bring back HM.  Silas voted for me cause i asked him.In the time that i made elder, I restored the ninja with wilbie, tinman,and bobo, restored the summoners with redsexy.  recruited and set up7 new Gm's, reviewed and opened 5 areas, coded a clan system, and fixed2 whole areas.  There is much more that needs done.  And i log on everyday to find some social archwizard speaking down from above.  Or activeones talking down about me or to me.  Telling me what is wrong with me, and refusing to listen to all the facts established about what is wrongwith what they have done.  I have done archwizard work.  I was an archwizard.I have used elder position to help everyone on here, even the assholes.Many other wizards have been inspired to come back, but that momentum is dying.They have been put off, forgotten, while the ALL important archwizardssit back for a month to discuss things.  Redsexy was ignored for a year.Her area forgotten.  Bobo has done more coding than any other personat his rank, he is ignored and put off.  I don't blame him for cutting back.There are wizards that are banished and wanted to come back, but they areignored.  And Exos is still here even after the testimony of 7 or 8 peopleattested to his absolute wrongdoings.After the ninja guild was restored, players and wizards started calling fornew archwizards with my name being mentioned many times.  These people weretold point blank to shut the hell up.  I have no conception of whatyou arches have going on in that little room, and what bullshit ideas arefloating around.  But face it. One coding arch, isn't going to cut it.The mud blew up in sargons workroom, understandings were reached, Then ignored.That Tuesday came and went a month ago.  The old ways are no longer needed.Who is gonna help you put in the 100 level system? Airborne? Silas?Kryll?, maybe Warlord and Uglymoth.  Maybe Sauron when he comes back fromhis next extended vacation.  Hello, Tatsuo has the ability, and has shown it.The mantras of me being some evil son of a bitch won't work forever whenthey are demonstrably untrue.  You know what Redsexy is right, I am BOTH.I cannot fathom the resistance to the move when everything points to a positive.When there is a chance to remove the dead weight and move up the peoplethat are bringing back the players.  The momentum as you put it is starting to slipwith the players.  I can spark it back up.  I will claim responsibilityfor a large percent of the comeback that is started.  I give the rest to thepeople who have been ignored and put off.  From what i know, there arepotentially 3 mudlib level coders on the game besides you Mangla.Those are your archwizards.Tatsuo, Wilbie, and Sargon.Please stop bogarting the highest position in the game when others can fill those positions.  calling kryll to login hasn't made him come back and fix theplace. and saurons instant appearance also has done little but piss me off.Put the level where the level belongs.  With the people that code this place,and enjoy it.You want the 100 level system in, arch those people.You want the guilds running and balanced, arch those people.You want players coming back, arch those people.You want new players, arch those people.You want wizards coding and being helped with code, arch those people.You want Holy Mission back, arch those people.If you want things the way they were. Sit back and dicuss things some more withthe deadbeats that brought her down.Make some changes, shake the boat. Take action, make it fun.If not, I am outta here.  I have forwarded this to every wiz that gives a damn, and i will ask thatthese wizzes write their feelings to MANGLA and cc it to TATSUO.  I wanta clean and open debate.  I also ask that it not be sent to other archeswhose feelings may be hurt by it.  That is not my intention.  I i havespoken an untruth, let it be known.  If i am right, tell mangla to fix theplace.Tatsuo, for Holy Mission**akira**To: manglaSubj: mailCc: tatsuoDate: Mar 22I recently reseved a letter that had some stronge statements made in it.Odds are you know the one I am talking about. We stand at a cross roads,it is no secret that this mud is dead, but there is hope. Recently the oldcoders have returned, and with them some new players. This mud can begreat once again. \"These are the time that try mens souls\" Henry V. Isay that because people don't seem to like change, it seems to try theresouls. Well its time to put the games aside and start to do what is bestfor the mud. Tatsuo has shown that he can get things done. Why then dowe not let him do this. The answer would seem to be with the arches. I haveno clue what you guys do, but I see what you don't do, and this is helpthis place. We need new arches and new changes to be made. I FULLY suportthe ideas set forth by Tatsuo and some of the others wizes. Given thisI stand with them and or walk with them, please let it be the former thanthe latter.                                       Akira**psi**To: manglaSubj: Tatsuo / ArchwizCc: tatsuoDate: Mar 22Well I'm only a beginner, and actually this is the 1st MUD i've ever been on. And I may not know much about what all the details are, but I can say that Tatsuo is someone on here who I could immediately tell that he knew what he was doing.When there was a bug, Tatsuo fixes it. When we bump into each other, he converses with me. I constantly see him on here and he has never EVER said anything like \"Well hold on. I'm busy.\"Like I said, I'm totally new to MUDding. But once I met people like Tatsuo and Redsexy who were this friendly, I haven't even tried one of the other 500 muds on this list of mine. That should show how attractive this place is. And if all the other Archwizzes made it what it is today, I'm sure those two can help make it what it will be tomorrow.Like I said, I'm totally new to MUDding. But once I met people like Tatsuo and Redsexy who were this friendly, I haven't even tried one of the other 500 muds on this list of mine. That should show how attractive this place is. And if all the other Archwizzes made it what it is today, I'm sure those two can help make it what it will be tomorrow.Psi.**redsexy**To: tatsuoRe:   ArchoodCc: redsexy, manglaDate: Mar 22Everyone knows I am in a particularly awkward position on this one.  Let me startby saying this.  No matter how much we say that this is only a game, it isalso a great part of our lives.  I see the hours everyone puts in here andthere's no way any of us can deny that what goes on in the MUD effectswhat goes on in our lives.  I say this because everyone involved in thisdebate is a friend of mine, one way or another.  I hope I haven'tcome out as being too hypocritical in any of this.  I think I havestood up for what is right, and I think I have praised when praisehas been due and criticized when criticism is necessary.  But itis always the action I criticize, not the person behind it.So I will say here what I have said to you all individually. And I willstart by praising what Tatsuo has done for Holy Mission.  He hasturned the MUD around, that is undeniable.  I could go through thelist of things he has achieved (I'm sure he'd like me to do that)but we all know what he has done here.  He is a motivational leader,without him I doubt I would have hung around for so long.I will also agree that the coding effort around here was appallingup until a few months ago.  Now Tatsuo and Sauron narrowly missedeach other, but this much was obvious.  When Sauron went awaya LOT of projects fell by the wayside.  It was the finalstraw in my prolonged absence (alongside my area not being looked at)and I know one or two others who had stuff going on that couldonly be worked on with Sauron.  I think Tatsuo underestimatesSauron's ability to code and the amount of stuff that is ready toship.  At the same time, in doing the lib stuff, monk was neglected.Coding here falls into two categories: The visible and the invisible.Sauron was working on the invisible stuff RIGHT up till hisabsence.  He was putting in 18 hours a day here some times. And notjust socialising - far from it.  But there's no way monk should have been left to rot for so long so visibly.  Givespeople the wrong impression.And as for Airborne and Mangla in the period up until I went away -I can't really comment.  Mangla was working with me on jedi, Airborne -I don't think I've seen Airborne code anything since 1993.  Butmaybe he's the same as Sauron and keeps his achievements quiet?(actually that bit about Airborne - I *do* remember him recoding theBaal Rog quest).  But a revamped quest and new skills for oneguild do not a happy MUD make.  Everyone was lax because HM was dying.It took Tatsuo to wake some of us up to the fact that HM could begreat again.Tatsuo has livened up place, but in doing so livened up the arches.And now he too wants to be an arch.  But the arches have reservations.This is where it all gets a bit blurry.  I hear one story from one sideand then another story from Tatsuo.  I can understand the initial concern fornot making Tatsuo an arch.  He has a reputation.  He goes on crusades thatwear everyone down.  There are questions about his coding ability. You neverget a moment's peace when he is online.  And not forgetting the securityconcerns.  The fact he doesn't tow the traditional arch-line.The fact there are people he would remove within the second on promtion.And the biggest reason for Tatsuo not being arched of course.\"There are no arch positions\".  That brings me nicely onto Silas.What IS Silas doing now?  Why is he still an arch here?  OK I'm gonna staycalm about this, but I would like to know if he is going to be inclidedin the quarterly reviews.  Silas is one of the friendliest, nicestpeople on here.  But if he's not doing anything for the MUD (as far as weare aware) then I really think that should be looked at.I sound like Tatsuo's yes woman.  I have disagreed with him on many things.I sometimes find he exaggerates statistics and his charisma can sometimesborder on the edge of manipulation.  But if he says fifteen players wantsomething, he will go out and find those fifteen players who want it.And I'm not even saying Tatsuo should be your first choice arch.You all know I'm not backing Exos on this either, Exos is, for allintents and purposes GONE.Now let me bring this back round to me and my life.  You may thinkI got involved in this because I like stirring trouble.  Or because I likethe sound of my own writing.  That's not the reason I got involved at all.First I saw Tatsuo personally attacking Mangla and I didn't like it.Then Tatsuo explained to me why he was attacking Mangla and I saw hisreasons, but didn't approve of his methods.  Between us (and I hope hedoesn't mind me taking the credit a little) we worked that one out.But things exploded again when Sauron came in.  Again I'm seeing Tatsuofrustrated, and again I am getting mixed stories.  You know what?I've been here for eight years, I can barely remember what I got banishedfor, let alone expect anyone else to remember.  I'd love to get youall in a room together and tell me exactly what you've all told ME(er - make that tell each other what you've all told me).Communication is the key that is missing here.Tatsuo.  Look at what Sauron has done as opposed to knocking him for stuffhe didn't do.  Try talking to the arches without insulting them.Arches, the whole lot of ya.  Listen to Tatsuo.  Don't arbitarily threatenhim with banishment. Yes, I know I have suggested banishment myself.And I still go with that.  If you are not going to Arch him then banish him.You're going to say that you have listened to Tatsuo.  I know you're goingto say that you've had as much Tatsuo as you can take.  The thing is,as many different viewpoints of an event there are, there is only one set offacts.  Someone along the way is lying or seriously mislead in their beliefs.Everyone.  Please treat each other with respect.  Do not judge withouthard facts.  Do not launch into mindless attacks on each other.  I canhonestly say I haven't said anything to anyone that I would be ashamedof having distributed.  I will gladly sit in a room with you alland defend everything I've said here.If Tatsuo goes, and seeing as Exos is as good as gone, who are we goingto have left?I guess I'll start work on master.c now then?Red**sargon**To: manglaSubj: Tatsuo's mailCc: redsexy tatsuoDate: Mar 22Here are my thoughts. Basically this can be broken down into 2 parts.1.  Current status of arches and their contributions.2.  Tatsuo's desire to be Arch1.  The current satus of arches is not great.  We have two active arches and one who codes.  Mangla has been here through thick and thin and has taken a ton of shit from every direction.  I've had very few problems with him that haven't been worked out.  He has asked for my advice on issues and gotten it and he's given me coding help many times.  He is approchable and open to new suggestions that are workable.  He holds the highest credibility with me...i can't speak for others.  This is my experience with Mangla.In my view the single most important quality of being a wizard or arch wizard iscredibility.  People can be taught to code, but honesty and a solid recognition of right and wrong are things that one needs to have as a foundation.  Without it they should not be wiz or arch.  There are many things which have been promised and not accomplished and pinning the blame on Mangla is at once unfair and misdirected.  There are/were 4 other arches who also promised these things.  Mangla cannot be expected to bear the brunt of all of their shortcomings.   As I said, he has stuck it out and coded while other arches didn't.  To remove or want Mangla removed is arrogant and stupid.2.  Tatsuo asks that if he has spoken an untruth in his mail to us that we bring it up.  I won't say that he's delibrately misled, but I will say that he has distorted some facts, intentional or not.  First, Exos and I had been looking into the guild master problem for some time and i've approached Mangla concerning this problem even before Tatsuo was back.  I told Mangla that I would like to be GM of fighter guild and recruit Bobo and Wilbie to look into other guilds that have been missing GM's.  I wanted Red to do Jedi also.  Even though Tatsuo has done an enormous amount to get HM back and enstill enthusiasm here again there are things that others have been doing before and now continue to do...just because we don't post on every little thing we do doesn't mean it isn't being done.  So actually, Tatsuo exagerates the point of Gms.	Tatsuo also exagerates of the review of areas.  There were many of us involved in reviewing areas, specifically Redsexy's.  Not that Tatsuo didnt' contribute to this, more or less than others, but his point is that HE did it alone.  This is also an exageration.	Ask yourself this;  If someone told you 10 things and 2 were exagerations or false, and these things you know about, what are you to think of the other 8 things they tell you?  Credibility IS the issue.  Tatsuo may be capable of being Arch in technical areas, but he leaves too many questions in other areas.  He should be promoted to Arch only when he has demonstrated that he can be trusted to be stable and credible.  In my opinion, he must be able to work with Mangla.  He can do all these things.  When he does, I will put in my support for him as an arch.	As for the rest of the mail from Tatsuo, I will not respond.  I will only discuss matters of which I have first hand knowledge and won't get into dragging anyone in the mud.	These are my opinions.  SargonHope the format is easy to read...copying into mailer was a pain.**tinman**To: manglaSubj: TatsuoCc: tatsuoDate: Mar 22I think what tatsuo says is true.  the mud died because of all the changesand being a arch here you have responsibility.  And people who lack theresponsibility should be taken off arch immediately.  Once people seehow great hm was and what it really was.  I can even say i left hm becauseof lack of work being done and no one gives a damn about the mud but Tatsuocan make a difference.  He made me realized the mud can change.  Thereforei have help him with the ninja guild.  He show me many things that canbe added to improve hm.  I say why don't we just give tatsuo a try.  are you afraid of him??  if so, you can watch him and see his abilityto work. you will find your suspiouicans are wrong.  This mud will dieagain and make all the people here lost hope if nothing is being done.I have talk to a few people about hm.  they say the arch doesn't careabout the mud anymore and at the moment they have saw tatsuo makingchanges which made people come back.  and actually take a look at this place.Let us not neglect hm again.  Give Tatsuo the arch position.Tinman**tinman**To: manglaSubj: guilds.txtDate: Mar 22I was also working on the ninja guild, you forgot my name in thatdoc.  and i wonder if i can work on the druid guild.  --> Proposing.Tinman**nobunaga**To: manglaSubj: tatsuoDate: Mar 22I am a really old player of Holy Mission, was Jaer.  I have seenmany things happen on this mud.  This was my first mud have playedand it was so good in the beginning........Suddenly in the middlewith all the changes and the staff doing nothing.  I found outholy mission was getting boring and becoming bullshit.  Until recentlyi have come back due to the fact that something is being done.The arches gives promise which they never live up to.  (some even)like the ninja guild being fixed and stuff.  I have found out Tatsuowould make a great arch since he is willing to spend time for this mudwhich a lot of 