aken care of in its owntime also. There are many many facts that have beenleft out. There are no insecurity issues.-Manglaarches**wilbie**To: manglaSubj: this arch stuffCc: sargon, akira, uruz, tatsuo, bobo, tinman, redsexy, airborneDate: Mar 22Leaving all personal issues aside, and leaving all political bullshit aside,I think Tatsuo and the others who have spoken up have some good points.Whether that means new arches or just new roles for lower levels, the factremains that we need change.Right now we have one active arch.  In order to accomplish everything that needs to be done here, that just won't do.  We either need new arches or thearches need to pass on some roles to the elders.  It's very simple.This is not a rip on Airborne, or any other arch.  Actually, let me rephrasethat part...  This is not a rip on Airborne, but it IS a rip on the others.Airborne still logs in, and he still makes a visible effort.  But the factremains that Mangla is the only arch who plays a primary role in Holy Mission.Mangla makes the decisions.  Mangla makes the policy.  Airborne acts as sortof a check - just to keep things balanced.As for the other arches, how in the hell can a person be considered an archwhen they never log on and do anything?  Popping in now and then to vote onsomething that you don't even care about doesn't count.This is also not a rip on Mangla.  Personally, I have no problem with Mangla.The problem I have is that Mangla (purposely or not) has placed the entireMud on his shoulders.  One person just doesn't cut it.  It doesn't matter ifyou have the best intentions in the world.  One person does not make a mud.Personally, I think Tatsuo would make a very good arch.  Quite frankly, I think a great number of the people we have right now would make great arches.Let's stop thinking of the \"arch\" position as some elite rank.  It's just another level with more work involved.  If someone has the ability, and thedesire, they should be given the opportunity to do the work.  They certainly have more business with that rank than someone who neverlogs in.One last thing, for the record.  I don't want to be an arch.  If raising mylevel will help me help this mud then yes, I'm all for promotion.  Promoteme to whatever I can best help you with.  To me, that's all rank is.  It'saccess to do more good for the Mud.**tetsuhara**To: tatsuoSubj: ArchoodCc: manglaDate: Mar 22well....lots of things said in all that.......having been a player for the better part of six years i think i've seen a lotof what's gone on from the players perspective..... although this doesn'tgive me authority to say whats gone on behind the scenes as it were, itsstill painfully obvious to anyone who plays for an extended period that thingsaren't running as smoothly as they should.....from the point of view of the work done by wizzes, elders and arches.... thereis definitely a trend towards who is actually working and who is on for the moresocial aspects of the mud...credit given where its due... given the amount of time elapsed since tatsuo'sbanning and subsequent re-instatement (well almost) isn't it obvious that  the fears of wrong-doing were ill-founded?on the subject of propsing wizzes or elders that should be arches... i mustadmit that i was more than a little peeved at being slapped down for the suggestion.....considering that a lot of players log far more time on the mud at the momentwould'n't it make sense to take on board suggestions rather than dismissingthem out of hand?  one would almost think that these players didn't have theexperience and the prior knowledge of the way the mud operates to make asimple nomination......anyway.... there's some more two-cents worth of opinion......tets.**widge**To: manglaSubj: Tatsuo 4 archCc: tatsuoDate: Mar 23Dear ManglaWell having read all that Tats had to say, I can honestly back him up for the position of arch wiz. Like Psi