gree that without a GOOD reason, no item should be allowed to exceed them.i would, however, suggest that higher be allowed on specific mobsexample:  a ring with a 3 armor class, but a - 3 light level.a sword that has a 30 weapon class but does 10 damage a round to its wieldera staff that hits a mob for a max of 100, but has a 5% chance of hitting it for 200, and wielder for 50As is, the wand may be possible, but the others are not.I am not suggesting the 'caps' be removed from max wc and ac, juston a case by case basis, they be allowed to be exceededAlso, regarding armor.Allow an armor type to be multi-type example: (a suit of FULL PLATE that includes gauntlets and boots and a helmet.these items dont even need to exceed legal maximums when totaled, butit would be one item that provided the combined AC for all four items (armor, glove, boot, helmet).I have to go, so maybe more later.Anla'shok Na Turbo, master of 1000 bugs.**redsexy**To: manglaFwd:  StrikeDate: Mar 27To: redsexySubj: StrikeCc: sargon, shadowmonk, nae, bobo, nunu, turbo, tinman, thumper, akira, nylakoorubDate: Mar 27I propose a coding strike, to let the arches know that we are not going toput up with their shit anymore.  They have had THREE YEARS to get this mudback together, and so far they've failed miserably.  Furthermore, they'veallowed personal vandettas to hinder the progress of the mud.I suggest the following conditions to begin coding again:1.  Reinstate Tatsuo.  That's a given.  He's done more for this mud in a    month than all of the arches did in three years.2.  Demote ALL inactive arches.  Kryll, Magnal, Sauron, Airborne.  These four    have done nothing for three years.  Sauron has been \"working on the lib\",    Airborne comes in to read boards, and Kryll hasn't done shit.  As for    Magnal - who the hell is Magnal?  3.  Mangla must either step down from arch or promote at    LEAST one more arch in order to balance the power.If you 